# Manahil Sabir Portfolio — Project Documentation

This is the complete reference for how your portfolio is built, so you can change anything —
copy, colors, sections, the hero animation — without having to ask someone to do it for you.
Drop this file straight into your project root (e.g. as `DOCUMENTATION.md`) and keep it there.

---

## 1. The one rule that explains almost everything

**Text lives in `src/data/content.js`. Layout lives in components. Styling lives in `src/index.css`.**

Every job, standard, certification, project, and word of copy on the site is a plain
JavaScript value exported from `content.js`. Components (`.jsx` files) don't contain your
words — they contain `.map()` loops that read `content.js` and turn each entry into HTML.
This means:

- Adding a job, a cert, a project, a standard = editing an array in `content.js`. No JSX
  knowledge needed.
- Changing how a section *looks* (spacing, layout, animation) = editing the matching
  `.jsx` file in `src/components/sections/`.
- Changing *colors, fonts, spacing rules* globally = editing `src/index.css`.

If you only remember one thing from this document, remember that split.

