## 2. Tech stack

- **React 19** — component library, no routing (it's a single scrolling page).
- **Vite** — the build tool / dev server. Fast local reloads, bundles for production.
- **Plain CSS** (`src/index.css`) — no Tailwind, no CSS-in-JS. Just CSS custom properties
  (variables) for theming, plain classes for everything else.
- **No backend** — this is a static site. The "contact form" opens the visitor's email
  client directly (see §8) rather than calling a server, so there's nothing to host or pay
  for beyond static file hosting (Vercel, Netlify, GitHub Pages all work for free).

### Commands

```bash
npm install        # one-time setup — installs React, Vite, etc. into node_modules/
npm run dev        # starts a local dev server (usually http://127.0.0.1:5173) with hot reload
npm run build      # builds the production site into dist/ — this is what you deploy
npm run preview    # serves the dist/ build locally so you can sanity-check it
npm run lint       # runs oxlint (a fast linter) to catch obvious JS mistakes
```

You need Node.js installed (v18+) for any of this to work. `node -v` in a terminal tells you
if you have it.

