## 4. `content.js` field-by-field reference

Every export below is an array or object you can safely edit. Adding a new entry to an array
(a new job, a new cert) just means copying an existing `{ ... }` block, changing its values,
and adding a comma — React will render it automatically.

### `profile`
Your name, title, tagline, contact details, and the `socials` array (each entry needs a
`platform`, `url`, `icon` — see `Icons.jsx` for valid icon names — and `label`). **An entry
with an empty `url` is automatically hidden**, so you can leave GitHub/Twitter blank if you
don't want them shown.

### `grcPillars`
The three cards in the "How I Work" block (Governance / Risk / Compliance) — each has a
`name`, `tagline`, `description`, and an `accent` color. These are also what the pillar
filter buttons and colored tags pull their labels from.

### `about`
`paragraphs` (your bio, one string per paragraph) and `highlights` (the 4 stat cards — each
needs `value` (what's displayed, e.g. `"8+"`), `numericValue` (the number `AnimatedCounter`
counts up to, e.g. `8`), `suffix` (e.g. `"+"` or `"%"`), `label`, and `note`).

### `experience`
An array of jobs, **most recent first**. Each job has `role`, `company`, `period`, a
top-level `pillar` (used for the timeline dot color), a `summary`, and a `bullets` array
where **each bullet has its own `pillar`** — this is what lets one job show a mix of
governance/risk/compliance tags on different bullet points.

### `standards`
The table in the Skills section. Each entry: `code` (e.g. `"ISO/IEC 27001"`), `name`,
`pillar`, `scope`, `note`. Add a new standard by adding a new object here — it'll
automatically show up in the "All" view and whichever pillar filter matches.

### `methodology`
The 4-step process stepper. `steps` is an array of `{ step, title, pillar, timeframe,
description, deliverables[] }`. Add/remove/reorder steps by editing this array — the
stepper UI just renders whatever's here.

### `artifacts`
The documentation/evidence gallery cards. Each `items[]` entry: `title`, `pillar`,
`standard`, `badge`, `summary`, `highlight`, `format`, `tags[]`.

### `maturitySnapshot`
The 5-domain scorecard. Each `domains[]` entry: `domain`, `level` (current score),
`maxLevel` (usually `5`), `levelLabel`, `pillar`, `summary`. Change `level` to update your
self-rating for that domain.

### `projects`
Case-study cards. Each entry: `title`, `tag`, `pillar`, `problem`, `action`, `result`. Keep
this problem → action → result shape — it's the format hiring managers scan fastest.

### `certifications` / `continuousLearning`
`certifications[]`: `name`, `issuer`, `year`, `status` (`'Certified'` or `'In Progress'` —
this drives the badge color), `pillar`, `id`. `continuousLearning[]`: `title`, `type`,
`details` — for courses/communities you're currently engaged in rather than credentials
you've completed.

### `education`
Array of `{ degree, school, period, note }`.

### `skillGroups`
The chip grid near the bottom of Skills. Each entry: `category` + an `items` array of
plain strings.

### `navLinks`
Controls the floating nav pill **and must stay in sync with the `id="..."` on each
`<section>`** in the section components. If you rename a nav link's `id`, update the
matching section's `id` too (or the nav link/scrollspy will silently stop working for that
section).

