## 6. Design system (`src/index.css`)

Everything visual is driven by CSS variables defined once at the top of `index.css` inside
`:root { ... }`. Change a variable there and it updates everywhere it's used — you should
almost never need to hunt down and change a color in ten different places.

Key tokens:

| Variable | What it controls |
|---|---|
| `--bg` | Hero background color (currently `#4B2E83`, deep purple) |
| `--accent` | The single accent color reused everywhere: buttons, tags, timeline dots, badges, section labels |
| `--paper` / `--paper-alt` | The two alternating light background shades used for content sections below the hero |
| `--ink` / `--ink-70` / `--ink-50` | Text colors at full/70%/50% opacity, for headings vs. body vs. muted text |
| `--line` | The subtle border color used on cards and table rows |
| `--font-sans` | The body typeface (Inter) |

Sections follow a repeating pattern in the markup: `<section className="section" id="...">`
(or `.section-alt` to use the alternate background shade) wrapping a `<div
className="section-inner">` that caps the content width and centers it. Copy this pattern
for any new section you add so spacing stays consistent.

**Animations respect accessibility**: `useScrollReveal.js` and the CSS both check
`prefers-reduced-motion` and skip/instant-complete animations for anyone with that OS
setting enabled. Don't remove those checks when editing.

