## 8. The contact form

`Contact.jsx`'s "Send Quick Message" form has **no backend** — there's nowhere for it to send
data to yet. On submit, it opens the visitor's own email client with a pre-filled subject and
body addressed to `profile.email`. This works with zero configuration on your end, but it
does mean the visitor needs a configured email client to actually send it.

If you'd rather have true in-page submission (the message arrives without opening anything),
sign up for a free form backend like [Formspree](https://formspree.io) or
[Web3Forms](https://web3forms.com), and replace the `window.location.href = mailto:...` line
in `Contact.jsx`'s `handleSubmit` with a `fetch()` POST to your form endpoint instead. Keep
the existing `name` attributes on the inputs — most of these services read submitted data by
input `name`.

