## 9. Common tasks — quick cookbook

**Add a new job** → `content.js` → add an object to `experience` (top of the array = most
recent). Give it a `pillar` and give each `bullets[]` entry its own `pillar`.

**Add a certification** → `content.js` → add an object to `certifications`.

**Add a case study** → `content.js` → add an object to `projects` with `title`, `tag`,
`pillar`, `problem`, `action`, `result`.

**Add a standard to the table** → `content.js` → add an object to `standards`.

**Change your name/title/email/resume link** → `content.js` → `profile`.

**Hide a social link** → `content.js` → set that entry's `url` to `''` in `profile.socials`.

**Add a whole new section** (e.g. "Testimonials") →
1. Create `src/components/sections/Testimonials.jsx` (copy the shape of an existing simple
   one like `About.jsx`).
2. Add a matching data export to `content.js` (e.g. `export const testimonials = [...]`).
3. Import and render `<Testimonials />` in `App.jsx`, in the position you want it to appear.
4. Add `{ id: 'testimonials', label: 'Testimonials' }` to `navLinks` in `content.js`, and give
   your new `<section>` the matching `id="testimonials"`.
5. Add any section-specific CSS classes to `index.css`, following the `.section` /
   `.section-inner` pattern already there.

**Change the accent color (without touching the hero)** → just change `--accent` in
`index.css` — this alone re-colors buttons, badges, tags, timeline dots, everything except
the hero's actual background/frames (see §7 for that).

**Reorder sections** → just reorder the `<Hero /> <About /> ...` lines in `App.jsx`. Nothing
else needs to change unless you also want the nav order (`navLinks` in `content.js`) to match.

